      "year": 2016,
      "abstract": "This dissertation seeks to trace Hegel\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s shifting attitudes towards Spinoza, and its significance for later interpretations of the Hegel-Spinoza relationship. In contrast to virtually all other approaches, it will be argued that Hegel\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s earlier defense of Spinoza in Faith and Knowledge (1802) was superior to Hegel\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s interpretation of Spinoza shaped after his break with Schelling. There is precious little in the Anglophone literature that compares and contrasts the approaches of the young and \u00e2\u20ac\u0153mature\u00e2\u20ac  Hegel regarding Spinoza\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s metaphysics. In most discussions, the young Hegel\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s views on Spinoza are mentioned, but only perfunctorily, and not granted a sustained analysis.  This hurts our understanding of Hegel\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s relationship with Spinoza in multiple ways, but it also obscures the deeper connections between these two thinkers made clearer in Hegel\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s earlier writings. | 207 page",
